From: Stoicoci Mihaita <stoicocimihaita@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] q706f: dts: rear camera VCM (DW9763 / GT9768) on CCI0 bus 0

The ov13b10 rear module has a voice coil focus actuator, but the board DTS
describes no lens node, so no driver binds and the lens stays at its rest
(infinity) position: close objects are blurry.

Evidence
  Stock DT overlay (dtbo17, fragment@44 -> cam_cci0):
    qcom,cam-sensor0 (rear, csiphy 0, cci-master 0, reset pm8009 gpio1)
      actuator-src = <&qcom,actuator0>
    qcom,actuator0: cci-master = <0>, cam_vaf-supply = pm8150a_l4 (PM8150L
      LDO4, mainline vreg_l4c_1p7), 2800000 uV, 100 mA load; no GPIO.
    cam-sensor1 (s5k5e9, rear aux) and cam-sensor2 (ov8856, front) have no
    actuator-src: both are fixed focus.
  Stock CAMX module configs (vendor/lib/camera):
    com.qti.sensormodule.ofilm_ov13b10.bin: actuator "dw9763"
      (ov13b10_dw9763_actuator, ofilm_dw9763_ov13b10)
    com.qti.sensormodule.txd_ov13b10.bin:   actuator "gt9768"
      (ov13b10_gt9768_actuator, txd_gt9768_ov13b10)
    Both carry the same 10-bit actuator init, decoded (best effort) as writes to
    registers 0x02, 0x02, 0x06, 0x07, 0x08 with data 0x02, 0x02, 0x41, 0x3f, 0x00,
    DAC maximum 0x3ff. 0x06 = 0x41 is AAC3 + prescaler 1 (the dw9768 driver
    defaults); 0x07 = 0x3f is the AAC timing set here.
  Mainline: drivers/media/i2c/dw9768.c (CONFIG_VIDEO_DW9768=m, dw9768.ko is
  installed for 7.3.4-power) drives DW9768-compatible parts; the generic
  "dongwoon,dw9768" compatible is used so either module variant binds.
  On 7.3.4-power: no i2c client on the CCI0 bus 0 adapter besides 0x36
  (ov13b10), no lens entity in the media graph, vreg_l4c_1p7 unused at
  1.808 V (no consumers).

Changes
  - vreg_l4c_1p7 fixed at 2.8 V (stock cam_vaf voltage; its only stock
    consumers are the rear actuator/sensor/eeprom VAF).
  - camera-lens@c on cci0_i2c0 (vin = vreg_l7f_1p8, vdd = vreg_l4c_1p7,
    aac-timing 0x3f), linked from the ov13b10 node with lens-focus.

Uncertain
  - I2C address: the CAMX binaries were not decoded far enough to read the
    actuator slave address. 0x0c (8-bit 0x18) is the documented address of
    DW9763, DW9768 and GT9768. The dw9768 driver does not touch the chip at
    probe, so a wrong address shows only as "I2C failure" / CCI NACK in dmesg
    when focus_absolute is set or the subdev is opened.
  - lens-focus makes the ov13b10 async notifier wait for the lens subdev:
    if dw9768.ko is missing, the rear camera does not register.

Needs a new boot image (DTB change). Not part of the normal series.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-lenovo-q706f.dts
@@ -395,6 +395,8 @@
 		/* Compensate Android's portrait-based sensor orientation. */
 		rotation = <0>;
 
+		lens-focus = <&camera_rear_vcm>;
+
 		port {
 			ov13b10_rear_ep: endpoint {
 				data-lanes = <1 2 3 4>;
@@ -404,6 +406,21 @@
 		};
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Rear module VCM. Stock CAMX: OFilm module = DW9763, TXD module =
+	 * GT9768; both are DW9768 register compatible (10-bit DAC at 0x03/0x04,
+	 * ring/AAC control at 0x02/0x06/0x07). Stock init: 0x06 = 0x41
+	 * (AAC3, prescaler 1, the driver defaults), 0x07 = 0x3f.
+	 */
+	camera_rear_vcm: camera-lens@c {
+		compatible = "dongwoon,dw9768";
+		reg = <0x0c>;
+
+		vin-supply = <&vreg_l7f_1p8>;
+		vdd-supply = <&vreg_l4c_1p7>;
+
+		dongwoon,aac-timing = <0x3f>;
+	};
 };
 
 &cci0_i2c1 {
@@ -785,10 +802,10 @@
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
-		// cam
+		/* Rear camera VCM (cam_vaf of qcom,actuator0 in the stock DT): 2.8 V */
 		vreg_l4c_1p7: ldo4 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l4c_1p7";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
